<BaseLayout title="About — Vu Truong Giang" description="About Vu Truong Giang (Zang Vu / @zvwgvx), student researcher in cognitive AI and systems engineering.">
  <header class="page-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">Background / research</span>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>I'm Vu Truong Giang, also known as Zang Vu or @zvwgvx. I'm an informatics-specialized student based in Ninh Binh, Vietnam, researching autonomous digital entities and building systems software.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section-block">
    <h2>Research direction</h2>
    <p>My research centers on persistent artificial identity and long-term agency. Through <a href="/work/aelia/">AELIA</a> at SENTIA Lab, I explore cognitive architectures involving perception, autobiographical memory, belief/world/self models, deliberation, affective appraisal, social relationships and Theory of Mind.</p>
    <p>This is experimental work on computational models of consciousness-like and social behavior, not a claim to have created consciousness.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-block">
    <h2>Systems & security engineering</h2>
    <p>My engineering work includes <a href="/work/rift/">RiFT</a>, an agent-assisted black-box web/API security research framework under RiFT Research, and <a href="/work/lattice/">Lattice</a>, an early-stage P2P networking project for heterogeneous compute and edge nodes. I also work on client/runtime performance and infrastructure through <a href="/work/opusmc/">Opus Client</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-block">
    <h2>Technical background</h2>
    <p>My tools and areas of work include systems and backend programming, ML/LLM integrations, cognitive agent architectures and security tooling. I use Python, C/C++, Rust, Java, JavaScript and Node.js, together with Linux, Docker, Git and SQLite.</p>
